>>
>> It does not look like it is the new write IRQ bugfix - that works fine
>> over 4.19.
>>
>> Still debugging...
> Hmm, I don't see this with my Debian userspace.
> What exactly is your setup/config?

Debian stretch + the openswitch runtime. Works fine with 4.19 and worked 
fine since 4.14.

The test is to cat something big to the terminal. If you just run it 
with xterm it does not show up 95% of the cases. In fact you may never 
notice it.

I use the changelog from dimngr (/usr/share/doc/dirmng/changelog.gz) for 
that purpose. It is 768k once it has been gunzipped. Any large text file 
(a few 100k) will do.

If you cat that with 4.20-rc1 using xterm you get terminal corruption - 
garbage shows up in the input buffer. Similar story with stdio fd 
console, but much easier to reproduce and the console can even hang 
during boot.

For comparison purposes, a console in plain 4.19 without the write IRQ 
fix will hang on that test (not always, it may take a couple of runs). 
With the IRQ fix it is stable - you can run it in a loop 24x7.

